{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_007_cost_adv_rank_smooth_clipnorm",
  "intuition": "By combining the scale-invariant normalization of cost gaps and the explicit clipping constraints from the top-performing parent, this crossover retains stable gradients while enforcing bounds on the margin and the scaled difference. Incorporating the weighted loss normalization ensures numerical stability even with outliers. This hybrid approach leverages the advantages of both parents: the scale-invariant normalization ensures robust training, while clipping prevents unbounded growth, leading to a more reliable and stable loss function.",
